WEBVTT

00:55:27.892 --> 00:55:30.018
I'll be with you
at the moment of your death.

00:55:30.042 --> 00:55:32.335
I was here with you
at the moment of your birth.

00:55:32.359 --> 00:55:34.234
There's nothing you can do to lose me.

00:55:34.258 --> 00:55:36.281
You can't fail. You can't do this wrong.

00:55:36.305 --> 00:55:38.264
You are infinitely, bottomlessly loved."

00:55:38.288 --> 00:55:42.994
And it's so interesting to me
that the opposite of fear in my life,

00:55:43.018 --> 00:55:45.717
in my emotional landscape,
on the color palette,

00:55:45.741 --> 00:55:50.812
the opposite of fear isn't courage,
the opposite of fear is love.

00:55:50.836 --> 00:55:55.717
And that presence, a sense of,
"I've got you," right?

00:55:55.741 --> 00:55:58.519
Which is the thing
that we'd all want somebody to say.

00:55:58.543 --> 00:56:01.133
"I've got you, and it's going
to be all right."